dal the next day."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Third placed " [:a {:href "/athletes/77934"} "Mickey Patterson"] " is noted as the first Afro-American woman to win an Olympic medal. High jumper " [:a {:href "/athletes/77790"} "Alice Coachman"] " won the " [:a {:href "/results/58812"} "first gold medal"] " the next day. However, it was later revealed that Patterson actually had finished in fourth place, as the finish photo clearly showed " [:a {:href "/athletes/64579"} "Shirley Strickland"] " crossing the line earlier."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "692"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/73711"} "Fanny Blankers-Koen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} "25.7 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "24.3 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "24.4 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "723"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/68816"} "Audrey Williamson"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "25.4 (1 h7)"] [:td {} "24.9w (=1 h2)"] [:td {} "25.1 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "668"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/64579"} "Shirley Strickland"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "25.8 (2 